Z||000001||Cheever2||03-23-2001||09:05 PM||||My wife was awake several hours before she really became conscious.  Only then did we realize she hadn't been "with us" the entire time.  Normally that's what <I>she</I> says about <I>me</I> almost every day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  ||||reg||6
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-23-2001||10:25 PM||||Luckily, mine are staying in.  They're coming in straight, dont hurt at all.  I have one all the way in right now, and another 1/2 through.  Just once and a while I get to teething like a baby, but no real pain.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||03-23-2001||11:04 PM||||Mmmmm, sodium pentothal...<BR>nightie-night!||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||03-23-2001||11:07 PM||||Good luck and i hope all goes well.<P>I keep avoiding the dentist because my 2 lower ones need to be removed.  But as long as they aren't hurtin me too much, I'm letting 'em stay!!  I'm not a big fan of any sort of surgical procedure ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaft||03-24-2001||12:17 AM||||Let me just say, the earlier the better.  I had mine pulled my junior year in high school and it was easy and painless. I made him put me to sleep and I woke up with a mouthful of gause.  A few minutes after waking up I was able to walk on my own and when I got home I started eating (pudding). If you get them pulled later in life they have to drill out part of your jawbone with the tooth and you swell up a lot more. On that note.....Have fun and good luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||jlhuber||03-24-2001||02:07 AM||||Dang, everyone talks about getting druged up/put under/what have you, and still feeling severe pain.  I was awake for all four in one sitting.  Took about 30-45 minutes.  They gave me the shots with the needles and stared pullin'.  Didn't feel a thing except when I got stuck with those freaking needles.  Maybe I have a high tolerance for pain, but from my experience, wisdom teeth extracts are painless.  <P>------------------<BR>--Jess--<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/blackeye2/double0smile.gif">   <BR>If you expect the unexpected, was it really even unexpected in the first place?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||03-24-2001||02:34 AM||||It depends on how impacted they are, as far as the pain factor goes.<P>Luckily my lowers never developed, but I had to get the uppers removed.  The first one came out 10 years ago while in the Navy.  It popped right out and I didn't feel a thing (but I milked it for time off work).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The other one didn't come through until 4 years ago.  It was a bugger!  The dentist had to cut my gum to create more room for it to come out.  Even with that it came out in several pieces.... the dentist whacked it with a hammer (at least that's what it felt like).  I needed 2 stitches and was in pain for several days.  <P>I made the mistake of doing this over my lunchtime......I don't know how I finished out the day.  I was in severe pain and was so drugged up that I was barely coherent.  <P>I can't remember what drug it was, but they were big blue pills.  I was supposed to take one every 4 hours, but only managed taking two......they made me sick and "loopy".  My then girlfriend asked me for the rest to help her with her migraines.  My mouth dropped when she popped 2 without any effect (I'm about 175 pounds and she was barely 100 soaking wet).  It seems she had/has an affinity for prescription pain killers (demerol being her favorite), but that's another story (and why she's a former girlfriend).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||03-24-2001||02:46 AM||||I guess that my mouth is big enough to hold the extra teeth because mine have come in with no problems. It is just kind of weird to be cutting new teeth at this stage of life. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnnyK||03-24-2001||01:28 PM||||Yeah, my Pops is a dentist, and he tricked me for one wisdom tooth. It had already half come in, and he's like "just cleaning back there....... &lt;pop&gt;..."  "Damn you!"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by JohnnyK (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Coconut||03-24-2001||08:24 PM||||That won't make you lose any "Wisdom", will it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Good luck, hope all goes well!||||reg||12
Z||000011||btoth||03-25-2001||12:26 PM||||Well... being knocked out with the IV was cool.  Nice and cold and then nothing.  Woke up with the gauze and the monitor beeping with my heart-rate.  (Which was a tad fast.. hehe.)  Where they pulled the teeth doesn't hurt at all, but my jaw is sore form being held open and my cheeks look funny.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Sure would like to be able to eat some real food though... jello and yogurt is getting boring fast! ||||reg||7
Z||000012||Standard||03-25-2001||06:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jlhuber:<BR><B>Dang, everyone talks about getting druged up/put under/what have you, and still feeling severe pain.  I was awake for all four in one sitting.  Took about 30-45 minutes.  They gave me the shots with the needles and stared pullin'.  Didn't feel a thing except when I got stuck with those freaking needles.  Maybe I have a high tolerance for pain, but from my experience, wisdom teeth extracts are painless.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought I was the only one who didn't get knocked out when I had my wisdom teeth pulled!  They just pumped me up with novacaine(sp?).. I brought my discman with me so I could listen to music and not concentrate on the teeth... didn't hurt while they were pulling it, just felt like they were trying to push the teeth out through the bottom of my jaw.  After the drugs wore off I got the nice dull ache for a bit..  still not something I want to do again.<P>When I had my first cavity they didn't use any drugs, just drilled it right out.  Guess I'm special or something..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||filthyscarecrow||03-25-2001||09:29 PM||||i had mine yanked 2 days before new years eve. they didn't hurt at all, but the following infection did. the problem was that i had 5 teeth (which is why i'm the wisest a$$ in all the land, hehe), 2 of which were impacted. the 2 bad ones got infected, which also wouldn't have been so bad if the damn dentist would have given me antibiotics for it when i told him it was infected. they didn't believe me. but i went out to the bars the night i got them pulled. they gave me vicodin and i just made sure to pop one ever 4 hours and i was just dandy. my landlady sed that having her wisdom teeth out was worse than giving birth. if that's the case, i don't think the girlies have anything to lord over us anymore! yeah, i know, i know. but given her analogy, giving birth sounds like a piece of cake : ) hehe...<P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000014||Loki||03-26-2001||02:50 AM||||Well, since im stupid and dont goto the dentist like im supposed to I went and got 3 wisdom and the 3 teeth beside those yanked in one day... Got the drug shot in the gums ALOT!!! But never out, just felt em tugging...Not pain hardly cause i was on extra strength tylonal like eveyry 2 hours   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And just think I have more caveties and need to go back..Just gimme my false teeth NOW!!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierogt88||03-26-2001||12:50 PM||||When i joined the marines, they sent me to get them pulled.  They decided to pull three of them and leave the bad one for after i was done with boot camp.  It took them all of three minutes from when i sat down to when i was out the door.  The pain killer started kicking in right about the time I got back to my platoon, just in time to join a 3 mile hike.  I still have the bad one...||||reg||1
Z||000016||bHooper||03-26-2001||01:27 PM||||<B>standard & jlhuber</B>... you are not alone.<P>i had all 4 of mine removed in one sitting, 7 years ago.  7 years b4, the doc told me "you will have to have those wisdom teath removed or they'll cause you problems".  well it took 6 years, and bunch of headaches later for me to give in!<P>i was wide awake for the whole thing.  my doc doesnt gass anyone out because they cant laugh at his silly jokes.  anyway, the doc was happy (he gets his rocks off administering pain to people), and i was happy because i had no more headaches!<P>good luck!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000017||filthyscarecrow||03-26-2001||06:08 PM||||i thouhgt the anesthesia was the best part. they put in the IV and said,"you'll start to feel kind of warm and you'll be asleep in about three min..."<BR>the next thing i knew i was awake in the chair after the surgery and i was drooling all over myself. it was a great time! i wouldn't do it again, but it was kinda cool. hehe...||||reg||1
